;; The Clojure host contract as DATA — the symmetric half of `python-host.edn`.
;;
;; An extension is a separate deps project that pulls the whole engine in as a
;; `:local/root`, so NOTHING stops it from requiring any namespace the engine has.
;; `com.blockether.vis.core` says in its own docstring that it is the ONLY namespace
;; an extension should import; this document is what makes that sentence testable.
;;
;; `:contract/internal-debt` is a FROZEN list of the internal namespaces extensions
;; already reach past the facade for. It may only SHRINK: export what the extension
;; really needs from `com.blockether.vis.core` and delete the entry. Adding a name
;; here is admitting new coupling to an unstable tree, so it needs a reason in review.
;; `clojure_contract_test` fails on a name that is NOT here and on a name here that
;; nothing uses any more, so the debt can neither grow silently nor go stale.
{:contract/version 1

 ;; The one namespace an extension is meant to require.
 :contract/facade com.blockether.vis.core

 ;; Where extension code lives, relative to the repository root.
 :contract/extension-roots ["extensions"]

 :contract/internal-debt
 {;; Required from `extensions/**/src` — shipped extension code.
  :debt/production
  #{
    com.blockether.vis.internal.attachments com.blockether.vis.internal.cancellation
    com.blockether.vis.internal.config com.blockether.vis.internal.config-spec
    com.blockether.vis.internal.extension com.blockether.vis.internal.external-opener
    com.blockether.vis.internal.file-picker com.blockether.vis.internal.format
    com.blockether.vis.internal.foundation.editing.balance
